## Summary

First concrete migration under [ADR-022](docs/adr/022-by-domain-folder-layout-for-ocale.md) (by-Domain folder layout for `@bedrock/ocale`).

- Move the wire code for `experience-icon/` and `experience-thumbnails/` (peer Resource folders) into per-shape sub-trees under `src/domains/game-internationalization/{game-icon,game-thumbnails}/`. The old peer Resource folders are deleted.
- Bind the moved Operations onto `UniversesClient` as Operation Groups: `client.icon.{upload,delete,list}` and `client.thumbnails.{upload,delete,reorder}`. The standalone `ExperienceIconClient` and `ExperienceThumbnailsClient` (and their subpath exports) are removed; consumers reach for one client per universe.
- Update bedrock CLI consumers (`universe-driver.ts`, `build-default-registry.ts`, integration tests) to call `deps.universes.icon.*` instead of the old `deps.experienceIcons.*`.
- Helper file renames: `tests/helpers/{experience-icon → game-icon}.ts` and `tests/helpers/{experience-thumbnails → game-thumbnails}.ts`. Integration tests under `tests/integration/resources/{experience-icon,experience-thumbnails}/client.spec.ts` move to `tests/integration/resources/universes/{icon,thumbnails}.spec.ts` and drive the consolidated client.

The wire requests, parsed shapes, and rate-limit operation keys (`experience-icon`, `experience-thumbnails`) are preserved end-to-end. Conformance tests under `tests/conformance/` continue unchanged.

## Why

Both Operations only act on `(universeId, languageCode)` — they are not in Roblox's published Features list and so do not qualify as their own Resources per the vocabulary in `packages/open-cloud/CONTEXT.md`. ADR-022 establishes the by-Domain layout that absorbs them; this PR is the structural migration that proves the convention works against one Domain (`game-internationalization`) before a forthcoming big-bang migration of the remaining peer-folder Resources.

Closes #293.

